publish-client-count-for-app-server

Lane: cross

Unit: coordinate-client-lifecycle-for-local-daemons

ChildPatch: publish-client-count-for-app-server

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema-snapshot

Purpose: Expose real connected app-server clients and a control-center Quit operation that stops the managed local daemon only when the requester is last and existing app-server sessions are idle, completing normal SQLite shutdown.

Requires: Unit:mixed/configure-trust-bypasses-at-server-start

Provides: Publish initialized client counts excluding daemon and backend probes; bind shutdown requests to the existing client connection; check last-client and globally idle eligibility without side effects before confirmation and atomically revalidate it on actual shutdown; return actionable refusals and request errors without disconnecting or adding chat history; provide callable TUI check and shutdown operations and an accepted-shutdown exit summary; retain app-scoped count observations across thread switches and clear them on disconnect. Drain accepted ordinary logs after normal producer shutdown, then explicitly close the native state-runtime and initialized local-history pools so SQLite can checkpoint and remove closed sidecars. Retain native message-board pools across thread teardown and await accepted board posts before their SQLite connections close.

Boundary: Native connection sessions, request dispatch, turn admission, recovery, forced shutdown and logging failure reporting retain their ownership. Disposable internal ephemeral work remains subject to native shutdown and cleanup without feature-specific admission hooks. Preserve upstream slash quits and ordinary key exits, embedded and remote operation, and ordinary disconnects. Count notifications do not enter exec output or the status line. Response-writer draining belongs to response recording. Control-center layout, action keys and confirmation or refusal dialogs remain with its interface consumer.

Verification: Protocol serialization; admission and global thread-status shutdown tests; managed-daemon integration for probe exclusion, disconnect survival, check-only eligibility without closing admission, other-client refusal, last-client idle shutdown and background-turn refusal; TUI callable check and shutdown results, preserved drafts and connections on refusal, native slash dispatch, exit summaries, global count routing and disconnect clearing. Log-writer and managed-daemon tests verify final queued logs, normal pool closure, closed sidecars and standalone database reopening. Local message-board tests preserve canceled-caller post completion and verify shutdown waits for final commits before standalone reopening.

CrossGroup: control-center


